A||||13||Eric||Holy moly.  It's a Fiero!||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||04-10-2001||01:29 AM||||Maybe it comes from driving a classy car, or maybe it comes from being a suave guy, but sometimes something happens to make me question my very existence.  For what I once considered to be an anomaly, is now seemingly an everyday occurance.  I'm starting to believe that I've been choosen for something grander than a life of ordinary.  The things I've seen and the experiences I've had make me realize that the Fiero isn't simply a car, a mode of transportation, but beacon of direction, a guiding light of inspiration and beauty.<P>I've lived my whole life thinking that God's face was of a human, but infinatly good in a divine way.  Now, however, when I picture God, I picture a Fiero of Holy origins.  A perfect Fiero shaped object emitting smoke and fire out of His twin exhaust pipes.  The sound of a choir of angles at full rev.  The hair on the back of my neck stands sending shivers of electrical signals to my six fuel injectors every time I think about it.  <P>Is this wrong?  I grapelled with this for months now.  Could my Fiero be a window into a heavenly world?  Is this just simple idolatry?  There is no answer worth listening to that you or I could give.  Not even the deepest thinking theologian could offer an expination into this phenomenon.  <P>I can assume you are all familiar with Jesus rays.  Metorological events that cast a beam of light downward.  Occasionally I can spot one shining down upon my Fiero from across a parking lot or while I'm standing some distance away.  The same thing is true for rainbows.  I don't know how to explain it.  Once I even caught a pretty girl doing a double take as I drove by.  Is this dumb luck, a freak occurance?  Perhaps.  But I contend that it is something greater.  Some force of divinity shining a light of hope, a glimpse of freedom toward the direction of my Fiero.<P>In closing, treat your Fiero as you would treat a truly sacred object.  Give it your veneration, because someday it may seal your eternal fate.||||reg||1
Z||000001||RedOktober||04-10-2001||01:53 AM||||does this mean I will be dying in my car? It is great to think of a Fiero as a gift from the gods...but have you driven anything modern lately? <P>The only reason I am still in love with the cars is that I can have 3 for the price of a few New Car Payments  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and still have change in my bank at the end of the month. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||04-10-2001||03:26 AM||||Ummmmm . . . <P>It's a car, not god.  But a Fiero is one god damn special car.<P>It still amazes me that GM could have built such a wonderful form of transportation.  It also amazes me that I can buy running Fieros for less than my PG&E bill (the electric company in most of California).<P>Corvettes hate Fieros, Ferraris think they are cute.  The Lotus Esprit's "minnie-me", the Fiero is the most fun you can have for one month's salary.  It also make commuting in heavy traffic fun.  It's a car to be seen in.<P>There has never been a better time to be a Fiero-phile . . .<P>||||reg||1
